  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-19 (in session): the owner adopted all recommendations of the 11-19 review (three read-only research passes over the ADRs, the spec and the code; record ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/after_fast_smart_test_grouping.md). For this item:\nQ1: an internal error exits 70 and a broken pipe 141, set once in main() for the whole CLI (spec L123 'no two outcomes share a code'; install-extras --check also uses 1 as an answer). Items 1 and 3 (wrong-typed --input record fields; io-boundaries / other --input commands given a missing path or a directory) go in the SAME PR as exit 2, or they land at 70 as 'This is a bug'. Q2: an empty claims file (0 bytes, {}, claims: null, claims: [] or no claims key) exits 2; load_claims keeps returning [] (test_claims_coverage_guard relies on it); measured today: rc 0, and --json prints plain text. Q3: max_chains < 0 exits 2 (measured: -1 reads violated). Q4: a non-string claim id or text exits 2 (measured: id: 5 emitted as int claim_id); allowed_sanitizers waits on WI-biraf (wire it and require a list of strings, or reject the key). Also: the cli.py module docstring (L134-136) still states the pre-#2203 exit codes; fix it in this PR. Release notes: label the exit-code changes breaking (10.0.0 precedent). Related, filed: WI-huhip (a full disk reported as internal error)."  # fcd7
